### Retry default-view rebuilds invalidated mid-build

**Severity:** `high`

If `_defaultViewGeneration` changes while `BuildDefaultViewCache` is running, the current fallback can return `rebuilt` even though it was produced for an invalidated generation. The invalidation notification may already have fired before this stale snapshot reaches the caller, so Home can keep showing an old pinned/recent-command layout until another unrelated refresh. Retry the rebuild when the generation changes and only return a cache that was installed for the current generation.

```suggestion
        while (true)
        {
            var existing = Volatile.Read(ref _defaultViewCache);
            var generation = Volatile.Read(ref _defaultViewGeneration);
            if (existing?.Generation == generation)
            {
                return existing;
            }

            var rebuilt = BuildDefaultViewCache(existing, generation);
            if (generation != Volatile.Read(ref _defaultViewGeneration))
            {
                continue;
            }

            var current = Interlocked.CompareExchange(ref _defaultViewCache, rebuilt, existing);
            if (current == existing)
            {
                return rebuilt;
            }
        }
```
